window.docContents[101].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Process.Overrides/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Process___Overrides":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Process › Overrides.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the computational proof and symbolic proof 6 headline theorems depend on it 89 of 156 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nDeclarations on this page (8)def Program.ofSitesstructure ElfSymstructure ElfShdrdef parseSymEntriesdef parseShdrsdef parseSymtabFulldef resolveSymdef overrideProgram\n\nSymbol-Keyed Hook Overrides for Whole-Binary ELF Judgments (Arm64.Trusted.Process.Overrides)* Layer / Role: Arm64 Trusted Computing Base (Role::Spec, definitions only, 0 theorems).* Purpose & Key Exports: Full .symtab parse (ElfSym, ElfShdr, parseSymtabFull), fail-closed resolution of function names to addresses (resolveSym, resolveAddrs), the address-keyed hook program (Program.ofSites), and the whole-binary judgment that replaces named functions by Lean models (ElfRunsToWithOverrides). ElfSym / ElfShdr stay public because the kernel-speed resolution checker in ProofLib/Process/Overrides.lean mirrors their parsers.* When to read: Read when auditing a whole-binary theorem that models some functions of the executable (extern stubs, verified subroutines) instead of executing their machine code.\n\n\n\ndef Program.ofSitesL31–39 ↗#Hook program for whole-binary runs: supervisor calls go to svc, and override f replaces the function whose entry point is the absolute address addr for each (name, addr, f) in sites. base = 0, so a site fires exactly when pc.toNat = addr (Program.externAt?). code is empty: process steps fetch from s.mem (Program.fetchMem).\n\n\n\nstructure ElfSymL43–51 ↗#One .symtab entry (Elf64_Sym): type = st_info & 0xf, bind = st_info >> 4.\n\nstructure ElfShdrL53–59 ↗#The fields of one section header (Elf64_Shdr) that override resolution checks.\n\ndef parseSymEntriesL61–74 ↗#Parse n 24-byte Elf64_Sym entries from sym, with names from .strtab. Fails on a name offset outside .strtab or an unterminated name.\n\ndef parseShdrsL76–81 ↗#Parse n 64-byte section headers from sh.\n\ndef parseSymtabFullL83–102 ↗#All entries (local and global) of the first SHT_SYMTAB section, and all section headers, with the same layout checks as parseSymtab. Fails if there is no .symtab.\n\ndef resolveSymL104–123 ↗#Resolve name to the address of a function: name must have exactly one .symtab entry (of any type or binding), and it must be STT_FUNC (2) with nonzero size, 4-aligned, in a regular section (0 < st_shndx < SHN_LORESERVE) that is SHT_PROGBITS (1) with SHF_ALLOC | SHF_EXECINSTR (0x2 | 0x4), and [value, value + size) must lie inside that section and inside one executable PT_LOAD segment of img.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 125–131): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.Process.resolveAddrs\n\ndef overrideProgramL133–136 ↗#Program.ofSites svc with each override (name, f) ∈ os placed at the address of name.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 138–152): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.Process.ElfRunsToWithOverrides\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Process/Overrides.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Process.Overrides/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Process___Overrides"}});